55
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:34,928
最后，我们将讨论缩放法则和模型选择。
Finally, we will discuss scaling laws and model selection.

56
00:05:35,150 --> 00:05:39,716
这有助于我们理解模型的性能如何随模型规模、数据和算力而变化。
This helps us understand how model performance changes with model size, data, and compute.

57
00:05:39,918 --> 00:05:45,124
到本课结束时，你将拥有一套清晰的战略框架，在编写代码之前规划 LLM 项目。
So by the end of this lesson, you will have a clear strategic framework to plan an LLM project before writing code.

58
00:05:45,408 --> 00:05:46,928
那么，什么是生成式人工智能？
So, what is Genetive AI?

59
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:49,796
生成式人工智能从大量数据集中学习模式。
Genetive AI learns patterns from large data sets.

60
00:05:49,888 --> 00:05:52,208
它是一种能够创造新内容的 AI 类型。
It is a type of AI that creates new content.

61
00:05:52,398 --> 00:05:56,004
这些内容可以是文本、代码、图像、音频和视频。
This content can be text, code, images, audios, and videos.

62
00:05:56,302 --> 00:06:00,260
这里的重点是，输出的内容并不是以同样的形式预先存在的。
The important point here is that the output did not already exist in the same form.

63
00:06:00,528 --> 00:06:04,528
模型是基于从大量数据中学习到的模式来生成这些内容的。
The model generates it based on the patterns it has learned from large amounts of data.

64
00:06:04,718 --> 00:06:07,268
这使得 Gen AI 与传统的 AI 系统不同。
This makes Gen AI different from traditional AI systems.

65
00:06:07,598 --> 00:06:13,316
传统的 AI 系统可能会检测邮件是否为垃圾邮件，推荐电影，或者将交易分类为欺诈行为。
A traditional AI system might detect whether an email is spam, recommend a movie, or classify a transaction as fraudulent.

66
00:06:13,728 --> 00:06:17,888
这些系统是处理现有数据，并对其做出预测或决策。
These systems are working with existing data and making predictions or decisions about it.

67
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:21,060
相比之下，生成式人工智能是根据提示词创造出全新的内容。
Generative AI, on the other hand, creates something new from a prompt.

68
00:06:21,358 --> 00:06:29,808
例如，当你要求 AI 模型编写产品描述、总结研究论文、生成 Python 代码或撰写营销邮件时，这就是 Gen
For example, when you ask an AI model to write a product description, summarize a research paper, generate Python code or create a marketing email, that is Gen

69
00:06:29,968 --> 00:06:30,756
AI 的实际应用。
AI in action.

70
00:06:31,008 --> 00:06:34,564
它不仅仅是识别类别，而是产生一个新的响应。
It is not just identifying a category, it is producing a new response.

71
00:06:35,278 --> 00:06:39,008
所以为了清晰地理解生成式人工智能，我们应该将其与判别式人工智能进行对比。
So to understand Genitive AI clearly, we should compare it with discriminative AI.

72
00:06:39,248 --> 00:06:43,888
判别式人工智能旨在对现有数据进行分类、排序或做出决策。
Discriminative AI is designed to classify, rank, or make decisions about existing data.

73
00:06:44,128 --> 00:06:48,288
例如，欺诈检测系统会检查一笔交易是高风险还是安全。
For example, a fraud detection system checks whether a transaction is risky or safe.

74
00:06:48,448 --> 00:06:51,172
垃圾邮件过滤器会检查一封邮件是否为垃圾邮件。
A spam filter checks whether an email is spam or not.

75
00:06:51,374 --> 00:06:55,168
推荐系统根据用户行为对产品或视频进行排序。
A recommendation system ranks products or videos based on the user behavior.

76
00:06:55,408 --> 00:06:59,108
这些系统非常有用，但它们实际上是狭窄且针对特定任务的。
These systems are very useful, but they are actually narrow and task-specific.

77
00:06:59,248 --> 00:07:00,528
它们不会创造新内容。
They do not create new content.

78
00:07:00,688 --> 00:07:04,580
它们分析输入并给出一个决策、标签、分数或建议。
They analyze the input and give a decision, label, score, or recommendation.

79
00:07:04,928 --> 00:07:07,300
这就是为什么它们被称为判别式系统。
And this is why they are called discriminative systems.

80
00:07:07,598 --> 00:07:09,248
生成式人工智能的工作方式不同。
Generative AI works differently.

81
00:07:09,358 --> 00:07:10,688
它生成新的输出。
It generates new output.

82
00:07:10,768 --> 00:07:15,968
它可以写一段话、创建代码、回答问题、总结文档或生成图像。
It can write a paragraph, create code, answer a question, summarize a document, or generate an image.

83
00:07:16,206 --> 00:07:17,488
所以核心区别很简单。
So the key difference is simple.

84
00:07:17,678 --> 00:07:21,316
判别式人工智能负责分类或预测，而生成式人工智能负责创作。
Discriminative AI classifies or predicts while generative AI creates.

85
00:07:21,998 --> 00:07:25,088
LLM 是生成式人工智能中最重要的类别之一。
LLMs are one of the most important categories within generative AI.

86
00:07:25,168 --> 00:07:25,808
让我们看看原因。
Let's see why.

87
00:07:26,030 --> 00:07:29,636
LLM 是在海量文本数据上训练的神经网络。
An LLM is a neural network trained on enormous amount of text data.

88
00:07:29,808 --> 00:07:32,768
它的主要目的是理解并生成人类语言。
Its main purpose is to understand and generate human language.

89
00:07:33,008 --> 00:07:35,556
“大”这个词是指这些模型的规模。
The word large refers to the scale of these models.

90
00:07:35,822 --> 00:07:40,164
现代 LLM 可能包含数十亿个参数，并在数万亿个标记上进行训练。
Modern LLMs can contain billions of parameters and are trained on trillions of tokens.

91
00:07:40,494 --> 00:07:43,492
一个标记可以是一个词、单词的一部分或者标点符号。
A token can be a word, part of a word or punctuation.

92
00:07:43,758 --> 00:07:48,288
在训练过程中，模型通过不断预测下一个标记来学习语言模式。
During training, the model learns language patterns by repeatedly predicting the next token.

93
00:07:48,558 --> 00:07:53,860
因为 LLM 是在如此庞大且多样化的文本数据上训练的，它们可以执行许多基于语言的任务。
Because LLMs are trained on such large and diverse text data, they can perform many language-based tasks.

94
00:07:54,318 --> 00:08:01,316
它们可以回答问题、解释概念、总结文档、翻译语言、编写代码、调试代码并创作内容。
They can answer questions, explain concepts, summarize documents, translate languages, write code, debug code, and create content.

95
00:08:01,678 --> 00:08:04,260
这使得它们在企业系统中非常有用。
This makes them extremely useful in enterprise systems.

96
00:08:04,846 --> 00:08:06,528
那么，为什么这些 LLM 如此强大呢？
So why these LLMs are so powerful?

97
00:08:06,894 --> 00:08:09,088
LLM 的强大之处在于它们的通用性。
LLMs are powerful because of their generality.

98
00:08:09,248 --> 00:08:13,188
只要有正确的提示词引导，一个模型就能执行许多不同的任务。
A single model can perform many different tasks when guided with the right prompt.

99
00:08:13,488 --> 00:08:21,284
同一个模型可以编写法律合同、调试 Python 代码、总结研究论文、翻译段落或解释复杂的概念。
The same model can write a legal contract, debug Python code, summarize a research paper, translate a paragraph, or explain a difficult concept.

100
00:08:21,488 --> 00:08:24,356
这种灵活性并不是通过逐项任务明确编程出来的。
This flexibility was not explicitly programmed task by task.

101
00:08:24,528 --> 00:08:25,888
它是从规模中产生的。
It emerges from scale.

102
00:08:26,062 --> 00:08:33,316
当模型在海量文本数据上进行训练时，它会学习语法、事实、推理模式、写作风格以及概念之间的关系。
When a model is trained on massive text data, it learns grammar, facts, reasoning patterns, writing styles, and relationships between the concepts.

103
00:08:33,648 --> 00:08:36,740
这就是为什么它可以通过提示词适应不同的使用场景。
And that is why it can adapt to different use cases through prompts.

104
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:40,015
这就是 LLM 在现代 AI 中如此有价值的原因。
This is what makes LLM so valuable in modern AI.

105
00:08:40,256 --> 00:08:49,856
团队不需要为每个细小的任务构建一个独立的模型，而是可以使用一个强大的语言模型，并通过提示词、示例、微调或基于检索的系统来引导它。
Instead of building a separate model for every small task, teams can use one powerful language model and guide it using prompts, examples, fine-tuning, or retrieval-based systems.

106
00:08:50,190 --> 00:08:52,228
所以，生成式人工智能并不局限于文本。
So generative AI is not limited to text.

107
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:55,776
针对不同类型的内容，有不同类别的生成模型。
There are different categories for generative models for different types of content.

108
00:08:56,078 --> 00:09:02,180
大语言模型用于写作、摘要、翻译、编程和问答等基于文本的任务。
Large language models are used for text-based tasks like writing, summarization, translation, coding, and question answering.

109
00:09:02,574 --> 00:09:04,896
扩散模型用于图像生成。
Diffusion models are used for image generation.

110
00:09:05,070 --> 00:09:08,068
这些模型可以根据文本提示词创建图像。
These models can create images from the text prompts.

111
00:09:08,462 --> 00:09:11,172
音频模型可以生成音乐或合成语音。
Audio models can generate music or synthetic voices.

112
00:09:11,534 --> 00:09:14,820
视频模型可以根据提示词或其他输入生成视频内容。
Video models can generate video content from prompts or other inputs.

113
00:09:15,118 --> 00:09:16,676
还有多模态模型。
There are also multimodal models.

114
00:09:16,942 --> 00:09:22,820
这些模型可以处理多种类型的输入，比如文本、图像、音频，有时还有视频。
These models can work with more than one type of input, such as text, images, audio, and sometimes videos.

115
00:09:23,056 --> 00:09:28,132
在本课程中，我们将主要关注 LLM，因为它们是许多企业 AI 应用的核心支柱。
In this course, we will focus mainly on LLMs because they are the backbone of many enterprise AI applications.

116
00:09:28,558 --> 00:09:31,012
现在让我们来了解 Gen AI 项目生命周期。
So let's now understand about Gen AI project lifecycle.

117
00:09:31,246 --> 00:09:34,212
每一个成功的基于 LLM 的项目都遵循一个生命周期。
Every successful LLM-based project follows a life cycle.

118
00:09:34,416 --> 00:09:43,012
这个生命周期包含五个主要阶段：范围与问题定义、数据收集与准备、模型选择、性能评估，以及部署与监控。
This life cycle has five major phases: scope and problem definition, data gathering and preparation, model selection, performance evaluation, and deployment and monitoring.

119
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:50,372
这个生命周期之所以重要，是因为许多 AI 项目失败并不是因为模型弱，而是因为项目规划不当。
The reason this life cycle matters is that many AI projects fail not because the model is weak, but because the project was not planned properly.

120
00:09:50,702 --> 00:09:54,148
比如问题不明确、数据质量差或者缺乏评估。
So if the problem is unclear, the data is poor or the evaluation is missing.

121
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:56,516
即使是强大的模型，在实际应用中也可能失败。
Even a powerful model can fail in production.

122
00:09:56,846 --> 00:10:00,576
另一个重点是，这个生命周期不是一条直线，而是一个循环。
Another important point is that the life cycle is not a straight line, it is a loop.

123
00:10:00,736 --> 00:10:06,436
部署后，监控会提供新的反馈，这些反馈有助于改进下一个版本的模型或系统。
After deployment, monitoring gives new feedback, and that feedback helps improve the next version of the model or system.

124
00:10:06,894 --> 00:10:10,500
这种持续改进的循环对于现实中的 Gen AI 项目非常重要。
This continuous improvement cycle is very important for real-world Gen AI projects.

125
00:10:11,086 --> 00:10:12,484
所以让我们把它们明确理解一下。
So let's understand them clearly.

126
00:10:12,686 --> 00:10:15,012
第一阶段是范围与问题定义。
The first phase is scope and problem definition.

127
00:10:15,296 --> 00:10:17,348
这是很多团队最容易犯错的地方。
This is where many teams make first mistake.

128
00:10:17,646 --> 00:10:20,096
仅仅说“构建一个 AI 聊天机器人”并不是一个明确的范围。
Saying build an AI chatbot is not a clear scope.

129
00:10:20,256 --> 00:10:25,856
更好的范围是准确说明系统应该做什么、使用什么输入以及期望的输出是什么。
A better scope explains exactly what the system should do, what input it will use, and what output is expected.

130
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:30,532
所以在使用生成式人工智能之前，团队还应该思考是否真的需要生成功能。
So before using generative AI, teams should also ask whether generation is actually needed.

131
00:10:30,894 --> 00:10:35,524
有些任务可能更好地通过分类、抽取或排序模型来解决。
Some tasks may be better solved using classification, extraction, or ranking models.

132
00:10:36,878 --> 00:10:40,496
生成式人工智能很强大，但它并不总是解决每个问题的最佳工具。
Generative AI is powerful, but it's not always the guide tool for every problem.

133
00:10:40,718 --> 00:10:42,896
第二阶段是数据收集与准备。
The second phase is data gathering and preparation.

134
00:10:43,150 --> 00:10:44,896
数据的要求取决于采用的方法。
The data requirement depends on the approach.

135
00:10:45,198 --> 00:10:47,776
提示工程可能只需要一个好的提示词和一些示例。
Prompt engineering may need only a good prompt and examples.

136
00:10:48,078 --> 00:10:50,176
微调需要指令与响应对。
Fine-tuning needs instruction response pairs.

137
00:10:50,416 --> 00:10:52,388
RAG systems 需要一个干净的知识库。
RAC systems need a clean knowledge base.

138
00:10:52,656 --> 00:10:55,456
在每种情况下，数据的质量都比数量更重要。
In every case, data quality matters more than the quantity.

139
00:10:55,726 --> 00:10:57,616
接下来我们来谈谈模型选择评估。
So let's say about model selection evaluation.

140
00:10:57,856 --> 00:11:00,868
模型选择是任何 LLM 项目中的一个重大决策。
Model selection is a major decision in any LLM project.

141
00:11:01,056 --> 00:11:06,628
合适的模型取决于任务复杂度、延迟、隐私性、成本和定制化需求。
The right model depends on the task complexity, latency, privacy, cost, and customization needs.

142
00:11:07,054 --> 00:11:13,092
如果任务需要最强的能力且不涉及数据隐私问题，那么可以使用前沿的 API 模型。
If the task requires maximum capability and if the data privacy is not a concern, then a frontier API model can be used.

143
00:11:13,326 --> 00:11:20,132
如果数据隐私很重要，或者在大规模应用时 API 成本过高，那么自托管的开源模型可能是更好的选择。
If data privacy is important or if API cost becomes too high at large scale, a self-hosted open source model may be a better choice.

144
00:11:20,366 --> 00:11:26,016
对于医疗、法律或金融等专业领域，可能需要微调或特定领域的模型。
For specialized domains like medical, legal or financial work, fine-tuning or domain-specific models may be needed.

145
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:28,656
性能评估应该在部署之前进行。
Performance evaluation should happen before the deployment.

146
00:11:28,974 --> 00:11:33,316
团队应当衡量准确性、忠实度、相关性、安全性、延迟和成本。
Teams should measure accuracy, faithfulness, relevance, safety, latency, and cost.

147
00:11:33,678 --> 00:11:39,616
如果没有适当的评估，一个系统在演示时可能看起来很出色，但当真实用户开始使用时就会失败。所以
Without proper evaluation, a system may look impressive in a demo but fail when real users start using it. So

148
00:11:39,696 --> 00:11:41,316
让我们来了解一下缩放法则。
let's understand about scaling laws.

149
00:11:41,536 --> 00:11:46,884
它解释了随着我们增加模型参数、训练数据和算力，模型性能是如何提升的。
It explains how model performance improves as we increase model parameters, training data, and compute.

150
00:11:47,136 --> 00:11:53,220
这些规律帮助研究人员了解到，当模型按正确的方式进行扩展时，LLM 的性能可以以可预测的方式提升。
These laws helped researchers understand that LLM performance can improve in a predictable way when models are scaled properly.

151
00:11:53,518 --> 00:11:57,056
然而，Chinchilla 的研究结果表明，规模大并不总是更好的。
However, the Chinchilla insights showed that bigger is not always better.

152
00:11:57,216 --> 00:12:03,456
在计算资源有限的情况下，用更多的数据去训练一个较小的模型，往往比用较少的数据去训练一个巨大的模型效果更好。
For a fixed compute budget, it can be better to train a smaller model on more data rather than a larger model on less data.

153
00:12:03,696 --> 00:12:06,116
这改变了许多现代模型的训练方式。
This changed how many modern models are trained.

154
00:12:06,478 --> 00:12:10,436
核心要点是，我们不应该仅凭参数数量来衡量一个模型。
The main key takeaway is that we should not judge a model only by parameter count.

155
00:12:10,736 --> 00:12:17,764
一个经过良好训练的小模型，尤其是在特定领域进行微调后，在相关任务上的表现可以超过一个大得多的通用模型。
A well trained smaller model, especially when fine tuned for a specific domain, can outperform a much larger generic model on that task.

156
00:12:18,254 --> 00:12:21,216
是否符合用途比单纯的规模更重要。
Fitness for purpose matters more than the raw size.

157
00:12:24,016 --> 00:12:25,284
欢迎来到本课。
Welcome to this lesson.

158
00:12:25,518 --> 00:12:31,012
在本课中，我们将学习 Transformer架构，它是现代大语言模型的基础。
In this lesson, we will understand the transformer architecture, which is the foundation of modern large language models.

159
00:12:31,456 --> 00:12:40,176
让 LLM 变得强大的所有功能，比如理解上下文、生成文本、回答问题、翻译语言以及处理长句子，
Everything that makes LLMs powerful, such as understanding context, generating text, answering questions, translating languages, and handling long sentences,

160
00:12:40,336 --> 00:12:41,572
都源于这种架构。
comes from this architecture.

161
00:12:42,126 --> 00:12:46,628
我们首先看论文《注意力就是你所需要的一切》，它在 2017 年首次引入了 Transformer。
We will first look at the paper Attention is All You Need, which introduced Transformers in 2017.

162
00:12:46,736 --> 00:12:51,908
接着我们将了解分词和嵌入，它们能将原始文本转换为模型可以处理的数字。
Then we'll understand tokenization and embeddings, which convert raw text into numbers that a model can process.

163
00:12:52,256 --> 00:13:00,976
之后，我们将涵盖自注意力、多头注意力、位置编码、完整的 Transformer 块，以及三种主要的 Transformer 类型：仅编码器、
After that, we will cover self-attention, multi-head attention, positional encoding, the complete transformer block, and three main transformer types that is encoder only,

164
00:13:01,216 --> 00:13:03,268
仅解码器，和编码器-解码器。
decoder only, and encoder decoder.

165
00:13:03,630 --> 00:13:08,900
到本课结束时，你将理解为什么 Transformer 成为了现代 AI 系统的核心支柱。
So by the end of this lesson, you will understand why transformers became the backbone of modern AI systems.

166
00:13:09,614 --> 00:13:10,628
那么，让我们开始吧。
So let's get started.

167
00:13:10,896 --> 00:13:12,576
那篇改变一切的论文。
The paper that changed everything.

168
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:17,456
Transformer架构是在 2017 年的论文《注意力就是你所需要的一切》中提出的。
The transformer architecture was introduced in the 2017 paper Attention is All You Need.

169
00:13:17,696 --> 00:13:23,812
这篇论文成为了现代 AI 的基石，因为如今几乎每一个主要的 LLM 都基于 Transformer。
This paper became the foundation of modern AI because almost every major LLM today is based on transformers.

170
00:13:24,782 --> 00:13:30,180
所以像 GPT、Claude、Lama、Gemini 和 Mistral 这些模型都采用了基于 Transformer 的架构。
So models like GPT, Claude, Lama, Gemini, and Mistral all use transformer-based architecture.

171
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:34,976
Transformer 之所以变得如此重要，主要是因为它改变了模型处理语言的方式。
The main reason transformers became so important is that they changed how models process language.

172
00:13:35,136 --> 00:13:41,092
Transformer 不再是一个词一个词地阅读文本，而是允许每个标记同时查看其他的标记。
Instead of reading text one word at a time, transformers allow every token to look at the other tokens at the same time.

173
00:13:41,422 --> 00:13:45,892
这有助于模型更好地理解上下文，并让大规模训练变得快得多。
This helped models understand context better and made large-scale training much faster.

174
00:13:46,350 --> 00:13:51,012
这个理念也使得在 GPU 上高效训练更大规模的模型成为可能。
This idea also made it possible to train much larger models like GPU efficiently.

175
00:13:51,566 --> 00:13:55,136
在 Transformer 出现之前，语言模型通常使用循环神经网络（RNN）。
Before transformers, language models commonly used recurrent neural networks.

176
00:13:55,406 --> 00:14:00,256
循环神经网络按顺序处理文本，一个标记接一个地从左到右处理。
Recurrent neural networks process text sequentially, one token at a time, from left to right.

177
00:14:00,494 --> 00:14:05,028
主要问题是 RNN 依赖于隐藏状态来传递来自早期标记的信息。
The main issue was the RNN depend on a hidden state to carry information from earlier tokens.

178
00:14:05,296 --> 00:14:10,756
随着句子变长，来自开头的关键信息可能会变得微弱、被压缩或者被遗忘。
As sentences became longer, important information from beginning could become weak, compressed, or forgotten.

179
00:14:11,054 --> 00:14:14,628
这使得 RNN 很难理解长距离的关联。
This made it difficult for RNN to understand long-range relationships.

180
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:20,416
例如，在一个长段落中，末尾的一个词可能依赖于很久之前提到的一个词或一个想法。
For example, in a long paragraph, a word at the end may depend on a word or idea mentioned much earlier.

181
00:14:20,656 --> 00:14:25,668
RNN 也很难高效训练，因为它们无法同时处理所有的标记。
RNN were also difficult to train efficiently because they could not process all tokens at the same time.

182
00:14:25,998 --> 00:14:30,096
每一步都依赖于上一步，这导致训练缓慢且难以扩展。
Each step depended on the previous step, which made training slow and limited scalability.

183
00:14:30,350 --> 00:14:32,164
那么为什么 Transformer 改变了 AI？
So why transformers changed AI?

184
00:14:32,416 --> 00:14:35,172
Transformer 解决了旧模型的重大问题。
Transformers solved the major problems of older models.

185
00:14:35,376 --> 00:14:39,684
它们取消了严格的顺序处理，允许所有标记并行处理。
They removed strict sequential processing and allowed all tokens to be processed in parallel.

186
00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:43,332
这意味着每个标记可以同时关注到其他所有标记。
This means every token can attend to every other token at the same time.

187
00:14:43,566 --> 00:14:46,052
它没有像 RNN 那样的隐藏状态瓶颈。
There is no hidden state bottleneck like RNN.

188
00:14:46,286 --> 00:14:50,576
因此，即使单词在句子中相隔很远，模型也能捕捉到它们之间的关系。
So the model can capture relationships between words even when they are far apart in a sentence.

189
00:14:50,670 --> 00:14:54,756
因为 Transformer 支持并行训练，并且在 GPU 上扩展性更好。
Because transformers support parallel training and they can scale much better on GPUs.

190
00:14:55,182 --> 00:14:58,372
这是现代 LLM 成为可能的主要原因之一。
This is one of the main reasons modern LLMs became possible.

191
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:04,260
随着更多数据和算力的可用，Transformer 模型可以变得更大、能力更强。
As more data and computing power became available, transformer models could grow larger and more capable.

192
00:15:04,718 --> 00:15:07,556
因此，分词是 Transformer 处理流程的第一步。
So tokenization is the first step in the transformer pipeline.

193
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:12,096
由于计算机无法直接理解单词，文本必须转换为数值形式。
Since computers do not directly understand words, text must be converted into numerical form.

194
00:15:12,334 --> 00:15:14,256
分词器将文本拆分为标记。
A tokenizer breaks text into tokens.

195
00:15:14,416 --> 00:15:19,696
一个标记可以是一个完整的单词、单词的一部分、标点符号、数字或空格类符号。
A token can be a full word, part of a word, punctuation mark, number, or space-like symbol.

196
00:15:19,856 --> 00:15:22,116
每个标记都会被分配一个唯一的标记 ID。
Each token is assigned a unique token ID.

197
00:15:22,336 --> 00:15:29,124
例如，一句话首先被拆分为标记，然后每个标记被转换为模型可以处理的整数。
For example, a sentence is first split into tokens and then each token is converted into an integer that the model can process.

198
00:15:29,710 --> 00:15:38,500
现代 LLM 通常使用像字节对编码这样的方法，其中常用词可能保持为一个标记，而罕见或复杂的词可能会被拆分成较小的片段。
Modern LLMs often use methods like bytepair encoding, where common words may stay as one token, while rare or complex words may be split into smaller pieces.

199
00:15:38,926 --> 00:15:45,412
分词很重要，因为标记数量会影响上下文长度、内存占用、处理速度和 API 成本。
Tokenization is important because token counts affects context length, memory usage, processing speed, and API cost.

200
00:15:46,030 --> 00:15:49,380
因此在分词之后，标记 ID 会被转换为嵌入。
So after tokenization, token IDs are converted into embeddings.

201
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:54,336
嵌入是一个稠密向量或一组数字，用来表示一个标记的含义。
An embedding is a dense vector or a list of numbers that represent the meaning of a token.

202
00:15:54,574 --> 00:15:56,896
所以仅有标记 ID 本身并不包含含义。
So token IDs alone do not contain meaning.

203
00:15:57,070 --> 00:16:00,452
例如，分配给一个标记的数字仅仅是一个索引。
For example, the number assigned to a token is just an index.

204
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:03,748
嵌入将那个索引转变为有意义的表达。
Embeddings turn that index into a meaningful representation.

205
00:16:04,142 --> 00:16:09,828
因此在训练过程中，模型通过观察单词和标记在上下文中出现的规律来学习这些嵌入。
So during training, the model learns these embeddings by seeing how words and tokens appear in the context.

206
00:16:10,542 --> 00:16:14,788
具有相似含义或使用模式的标记往往会有相似的向量表示。
Tokens with similar meanings or usage patterns tend to have similar vector representations.

207
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:21,412
例如，与食物、技术、情感或地点相关的词可能会在嵌入空间中形成有意义的模式。
For example, words related to food, technology, emotions, or locations may form meaningful patterns in embedding space.

208
00:16:21,646 --> 00:16:27,716
在应用自注意力之前，嵌入有助于 Transformer 理解单词、概念和上下文之间的关系。
Embeddings help the transformer understand relationships between words, concepts, and context before attention is applied.

209
00:16:28,206 --> 00:16:30,960
因此，自注意力是 Transformer 的核心机制。
So self-attention is the core mechanism of transformers.

210
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:36,160
它允许每个标记查看同一句子中的其他标记，并判断哪些是最重要的。
It allows each token to look at the other tokens in the same sentence and decide which ones are most important.

211
00:16:36,334 --> 00:16:38,948
这很有用，因为含义往往取决于上下文。
This is useful because meaning often depends on the context.

212
00:16:39,246 --> 00:16:43,428
例如，在句子“那只动物没过马路，因为它累了”中。
For example, in the sentence, the animal did not cross the road because it was tired.

213
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:46,308
模型需要理解它指的是什么。
The model needs to understand what it refers to.

214
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:49,840
自注意力使用三个向量：查询、键和值。
Self-attention uses three vectors query, key, and value.

215
00:16:49,998 --> 00:16:52,400
查询代表一个标记正在寻找什么。
The query represents what a token is looking for.

216
00:16:52,590 --> 00:16:57,316
键代表每个标记提供的内容，而值包含传递给后续环节的信息。
The key represents what each token offers and the value contains the information passed forward.

217
00:16:57,742 --> 00:17:01,200
因此，模型通过查询和键来计算注意力分数。
So the model comprises queries and keys to calculate attention scores.

218
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:04,640
分数越高，意味着一个标记应该更多地关注另一个标记。
Higher scores mean one token should pay more attention to the other token.

219
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:11,520
这让 Transformer 能够捕捉到近距离词汇和远距离词语之间的关系，从而更好地理解上下文。
This allows transformers to capture relationships between nearby words and distant words, making them much better at understanding the context.

220
00:17:11,694 --> 00:17:14,372
那么，什么是多头注意力和位置编码？
So, what is multi-head retention and positional encoding?

221
00:17:14,606 --> 00:17:18,500
多头注意力意味着模型同时运行多个注意力操作。
Multi-head retention means the model runs many attention operations at the same time.

222
00:17:18,798 --> 00:17:21,796
每个注意力头可以专注于不同类型的关系。
Each attention head can focus on a different type of relationship.

223
00:17:22,126 --> 00:17:28,002
一个头可能关注语法，另一个关注代词，另一个关注语义，还有一个关注长距离上下文。
One head may focus on the grammar, another on pronouns, other on meaning, and the other on long-range context.

224
00:17:28,430 --> 00:17:31,780
这些输出被结合起来，从而对句子产生更丰富的理解。
These outputs are combined to create a richer understanding of the sentence.

225
00:17:32,686 --> 00:17:36,708
由于 Transformer 是并行处理标记的，它们还需要位置编码。
Since transformer process tokens in parallel, they also need positional encoding.

226
00:17:37,038 --> 00:17:42,560
位置编码帮助模型理解词序，因为在语言中，顺序会改变含义。
Positional encoding helps the model understand word order because order changes meaning in the language.

227
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:47,972
例如，“狗追猫”和“猫追狗”包含相同的词汇，但意义不同。
For example, the dog chased the cat and the cat chased the dog contains the same words but different meanings.

228
00:17:48,526 --> 00:17:51,556
一个 Transformer 块结合了多个重要的组件。
A transformer block combines multiple important components.

229
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:54,788
它始于输入嵌入加上位置信息。
It starts with input embeddings plus positional information.

230
00:17:55,182 --> 00:17:59,748
接着应用多头自注意力，让模型能够理解标记之间的关系。
Then multi-head self-attention is applied so that the model can understand relationships between the tokens.

231
00:18:00,110 --> 00:18:06,212
之后，残差连接和层归一化有助于保持训练稳定，并防止有用信息丢失。
After that, residual connections and layer normalization help training remain stable and prevent useful information from being lost.

232
00:18:07,054 --> 00:18:12,000
该块还包含一个前馈网络，用于进一步处理每个标记的表示。
The block also includes a feedforward network which further processes each token's representation.

233
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:16,480
许多 Transformer 块被堆叠在一起，每一层都在构建更深层次的语言理解。
Many transformer blocks are stacked together and each layer builds deeper language understanding.

234
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:21,440
底层可能学习基础模式，而高层则学习更复杂的含义和推理。
Lower layers may learn basic patterns while higher layers learn more complex meaning and reasoning.

235
00:18:21,742 --> 00:18:23,876
现在让我们来看看 Transformer 架构的类型。
So now let's look into transformer architecture types.

236
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,212
主要有三种 Transformer 架构类型。
There are three main transformer architecture types.

237
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:32,420
仅编码器模型适用于分类、命名实体识别、语义搜索和嵌入。
Encoder-only models are useful for classification, named entity, recognition, semantic search and embeddings.

238
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:35,200
仅解码器模型用于文本生成。
Decoder only models are used for text generation.

239
00:18:35,406 --> 00:18:41,520
像 GPT、Lama、Claude 和 Mistral 这样的模型都遵循这种风格，因为它们一次生成一个标记。
Models like GPT, Lama, Claude, and Mistral follow this style because they generate text one token at a time.

240
00:18:41,806 --> 00:18:48,292
编码器-解码器模型适用于翻译、摘要和问题生成等序列到序列任务。
Encoder-decoder models are useful for sequence-to-sequence tasks like translation, summarization, and question generation.

241
00:18:48,654 --> 00:18:52,260
编码器负责理解输入，而解码器负责生成输出。
The encoder understands the input and the decoder generates the output.

242
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:58,800
每种 Transformer 类型都有其用途，取决于目标是理解、生成还是两者兼有。
Each transformer type is useful for different tasks depending on whether the goal is understanding generation or both.

